1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:00,780
Right now, the sun

2
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:01,660
just went out.

3
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:03,190
But its last light

4
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:05,960
is still flying toward Earth.

5
00:00:06,530 --> 00:00:07,490
For eight minutes,

6
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,450
nothing seems wrong.

7
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:10,130
Mara runs a weather

8
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,640
station in the mountains.

9
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:13,800
At twelve oh eight,

10
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,510
the last light arrives.

11
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:17,270
Her sunlight sensor

12
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,030
drops straight to zero.

13
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,260
Then the sky

14
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:22,660
turns black at noon.

15
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:24,850
Streetlights switch on,

16
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,130
and the town goes quiet.

17
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,560
Everyone panics.

18
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,540
Mara packs.

19
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,280
A warm coat,

20
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:33,390
a radio,

21
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,130
and a jar of seeds.

22
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,420
And her dog,

23
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:36,930
Ember,

24
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:37,580
comes too.

25
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:38,630
She checks the

26
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:39,410
thermometer.

27
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,250
Fifteen, and falling.

28
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:42,540
Frost is already

29
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:44,010
creeping across the window.

30
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:45,540
In seven days,

31
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:47,260
it will be minus seventeen.

32
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:49,000
Rule number one:

33
00:00:49,030 --> 00:00:50,550
heat is the real clock.

34
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,650
She has seven days

35
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,740
to find a warm place.

36
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:59,530
Part two. The first week. Follow for part two.
